From ba788ffd8917970798e0a2e4cf83b88c4e489f07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joaco2382 <104966815+Joaco2382@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 11:03:21 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix: size "auto" orthogonal projections from 0, keep their
 declared size

Scenes with "orthogonalprojection": {"auto": true} were sized as twice the
farthest distance of an image from 0, as if scene coordinates were centered.
They start at 0 (an image centered at 960, 540 fills a 1920x1080 scene), so
the scene came out twice as big and the content sat in a corner (workshop
1341926663 and every gif scene: 1309424009, 1477353862, 1671718580).

- The size is now where the farthest image ends (origin + size / 2).
- An auto projection that also says its width and height (gif scenes do)
  keeps them instead of being measured.

Tests: AutoProjection (2 cases).
